[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
bobbin needs Apple II ROM images to run; they are not included in this
package, because they are not redistributable. You must supply them
yourself and place them at these paths:

  %%DATADIR%%/roms/apple2.rom         (Apple ][, 12k)
  %%DATADIR%%/roms/apple2plus.rom     (Apple ][+, 12k)
  %%DATADIR%%/roms/apple2e.rom        (unenhanced Apple //e, 16k)
  %%DATADIR%%/roms/apple2e_enh.rom    (enhanced Apple //e, 16k)
  %%DATADIR%%/roms/cards/disk2.rom    (Disk II controller card, 256 bytes)

You only need the ROM for the machine you intend to emulate; the
enhanced Apple //e ROM is used by default. bobbin also searches the
directory named by the BOBBIN_ROMDIR environment variable, and a "roms"
directory inside the directory holding the bobbin binary.

If you do not have these files, see the bobbin repository page:

  https://github.com/micahcowan/bobbin

Disk images are not installed either, for the same reason. bobbin runs
fine without them; supply your own when you want to boot a DOS or
ProDOS disk, and pass it with the --disk option (or copy it to
%%DATADIR%%/images/). The images shipped in the upstream source
tarball, which this package intentionally does not install, are:

  %%DATADIR%%/images/dos33primary.dsk   (DOS 3.3 System Master)
  %%DATADIR%%/images/dos33primary.nib   (same disk, nibble format)
  %%DATADIR%%/images/dos33init.dsk      (DOS 3.3 boot/init sectors only)
  %%DATADIR%%/images/ProDOS_2_0_3.dsk   (ProDOS 2.0.3)
  %%DATADIR%%/images/prodos242.dsk      (ProDOS 2.4.2)

These are copyrighted and cannot be redistributed.

EOM
}
]
